Fares in the South Hudur Metropolitan Administration, which includes [[Mazar]], are higher than in other administrations, reflecting the region's unique economic character as Burawa's only private-property area and its culture of taxi use as a status symbol. Fares in Sago-Dare and Lanwaley are lower, reflecting the role of taxis as a supplementary service in areas with less comprehensive public transit coverage.

Payment is accepted through the same fare card systems used for public transit, as well as through [[BuFulid]], the state-operated taxi-hailing app introduced by the [[Ministry of Innovation (Burawa)|Ministry of Innovation]] in 2018.

